  "assessment": "Eligible. The frozen TeX defines the three-Lorentzian-plus-linear model at lines 213-224 and reports every central parameter for the equilibrium and t = 0.4 ps branches at lines 227-233. The revised card now binds those branches to disjoint source-anchored pre-pump and pumped-at-0.4-ps conditions (line 521), while retaining the shared sample, temperature, trXAS geometry, and polarization conditions (lines 521 and 525). The unspecified convention of the parenthetical fit uncertainties is correctly retained as provenance rather than treated as ambiguity in the deterministic central fit. Independent evaluation at 1,001 omega values on [527.89, 529.70] eV reproduced the displayed model with maximum absolute discrepancies 1.89e-15 (equilibrium) and 1.78e-15 (t = 0.4 ps); endpoint predictions are respectively (1.05656169082892, 1.04641638166533) and (1.57044429987778, 1.00999436114008). The Oracle semantics are a deterministic evaluation of source-reported central fit parameters, not a fresh spectrum, replicate, or uncertainty sample.",
